WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.552
Module 6 sits between the classic NLP methods we already know and the retrieval and generation systems we

00:00:08.552 --> 00:00:10.272
will build next.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:15.932
In Module 4, we represented text as vectors and used similarity to compare pieces of text.

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:21.522
In Module 5, we used classic machine-learning models for classification.

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:28.302
Transformers keep the idea of vector representations, but they make those vectors context-sensitive.

00:00:28.302 --> 00:00:32.692
The representation of a word can change depending on the words around it.

00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:38.912
That change is important for classification, named entity recognition, semantic search, summarization,

00:00:38.912 --> 00:00:42.107
and text generation.

00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:48.067
The concepts we learn here will also make the next RAG module much easier to understand,

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:53.277
because RAG depends on Transformer-based embedding models and generative models.

00:00:53.277 --> 00:00:59.894
Think of Module 6 as the bridge from traditional NLP pipelines to modern language-model systems.
